WEBVTT

00:02.610 --> 00:05.636
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.746 --> 00:09.308
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.418 --> 00:12.683
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.788 --> 00:15.586
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:16.024 --> 00:19.153
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.262 --> 00:22.254
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.498 --> 00:24.159
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.267 --> 00:25.859
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:26.002 --> 00:30.736
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:35.346 --> 00:38.282
Peter, you sure you're allowed to
bring a baby onto the golf course?

00:38.383 --> 00:40.647
Well, Lois asked me to watch Stewie
for the afternoon.

00:40.752 --> 00:42.413
It's all right.
I don't think the club will mind.

00:42.520 --> 00:43.714
It's Cleveland I'm worried about.

00:44.022 --> 00:48.015
Peter, is this really necessary?
I can't hardly see anything.

00:48.227 --> 00:50.024
Hey, look. It's President Nixon.

00:50.129 --> 00:52.927
No, wait, it's a black guy. No, it's Nixon.

00:53.366 --> 00:54.594
Oh, boy. That was close.

00:54.700 --> 00:57.794
Will you please hurry up?
It's 100 degrees out here.

00:57.903 --> 01:00.202
You're a worse parent
than Britney Spears.

01:00.674 --> 01:02.301
I know, I know.

01:03.377 --> 01:06.608
Oh, the gift basket was not worth the trip,
not by a long shot.

01:07.781 --> 01:09.613
Oh, I got to get that. I'll talk to you later.

01:13.955 --> 01:16.116
- Hey, Joe.
- Don't say it, Peter.

01:16.224 --> 01:19.422
- I was just wondering...
- Peter, I swear to God.

01:19.528 --> 01:20.790
What's your handicap?

01:21.997 --> 01:25.865
Oh! Every hole!
That's a joke that just doesn't get old!

01:28.570 --> 01:32.063
God damn it! Come on, come on!
Shit, shit, shit!

01:32.175 --> 01:35.338
Come on, Glenn, come on!
Get your head in the goddamn game!

01:37.047 --> 01:39.642
Hey, do you think
it's time to talk to Quagmire

01:39.750 --> 01:41.775
about his anger issues with this game?

01:41.886 --> 01:44.946
A white man shouldn't play sports
in the first place.

01:46.891 --> 01:50.419
- Hey, hey, hey! That's a stroke!
- I just tapped my ball, Quagmire. Relax.

01:50.529 --> 01:53.327
Oh, relax? Oh, okay.
Oh, look, I just tapped my ball.

01:53.432 --> 01:55.627
Oh! Just tapped it again!
Oh. Oh. Tap, tap, tap.

01:55.734 --> 02:00.331
Oh, where is it? Oh, it's in the hole.
Eagle! Yay, Quagmire!

02:00.506 --> 02:02.804
Hey, Quagmire. You know it's not fun
when you're like this.

02:02.909 --> 02:05.275
You want fun, go home and buy a monkey!

02:05.378 --> 02:06.709
What does that even mean?

02:06.813 --> 02:09.339
I don't know.
Boy, we got a beautiful day for this.

02:13.087 --> 02:15.681
Hi, Mr. Herbert. Here's your paper.

02:15.789 --> 02:20.887
Oh. Sorry, Chris, but I'm afraid
I'm gonna have to cancel my subscription.

02:20.995 --> 02:23.020
Cancel? But you love this paper.

02:23.131 --> 02:28.296
Listen, I think you're a real nice guy, but
I've just decided to go with another paper.

02:28.803 --> 02:33.673
Hello there, Kyle. You look nice today.
I see you're wearing your big shorts

02:33.776 --> 02:38.179
with the baggy leg holes
that flutter so carelessly in the breeze.

02:38.614 --> 02:41.778
Here's your paper.
What are you doing here? Beat it, nerd!

02:41.885 --> 02:46.515
Thank you. Would you like to come inside
for a cupcake and a glass of wine?

02:46.623 --> 02:48.215
Shut up, old man.

02:49.894 --> 02:51.987
What's going on in my pants?

02:52.163 --> 02:54.996
Looks like we got
six more weeks of winter.

02:59.070 --> 03:02.040
<i>We now return to
Cutting in Line in Front of Italians.</i>

03:08.147 --> 03:11.083
<i>Copernicus, why don't you navigate
yourself to the back of the line</i>

03:11.184 --> 03:13.084
<i>with your feet and stand there
with your shirt?</i>

03:13.520 --> 03:15.488
Hey, Peter, how was your golf game?

03:15.588 --> 03:18.751
Well, Lois, you tied my golf shoes
a little tight before I left the house.

03:18.858 --> 03:20.520
Had to deal with that all day.
Thank you very much.

03:20.628 --> 03:22.357
Oh, my God. Look at Stewie!

03:22.463 --> 03:24.522
Peter, you took him out
without any sunscreen?

03:24.632 --> 03:25.621
Maybe.

03:25.733 --> 03:28.395
You know the sun is dangerous
for a baby's skin.

03:28.502 --> 03:32.462
Peter, this is more irresponsible than
when you fed your mogwai after midnight.

03:32.574 --> 03:35.839
Peter, didn't the little Chinese man
tell you not to feed him after midnight?

03:35.944 --> 03:40.347
Oh, come on, Lois. He's so cute
and he's hungry. What could happen?

03:43.352 --> 03:45.946
Hello, I'm Fran Drescher.

03:48.658 --> 03:50.285
Kill it, kill it!

03:52.696 --> 03:55.665
What the deuce are you are all staring at?
Is there something wrong with me?

03:58.702 --> 04:02.070
Wow! Look at me. I'm a young Eartha Kitt.

04:03.274 --> 04:07.574
"President Johnson, bring our boys home
from Southeast Asia.

04:07.679 --> 04:09.510
"It's an unwinnable war. "

04:09.981 --> 04:12.849
- My God, look at you.
- Oh, look at my complexion, Brian.

04:12.952 --> 04:17.048
I am hot. I'll be getting more sex
than that Wisconsin nymphomaniac

04:17.156 --> 04:18.589
who used to live upstairs.

04:18.757 --> 04:20.486
Oh, God! Oh, God!

04:20.593 --> 04:24.758
Oh, crap! Oh, crap! Oh, crap! Oh, crap!

04:24.864 --> 04:27.765
Crap! Crap! Crap!

04:30.637 --> 04:32.265
Oh, crap.

04:35.543 --> 04:39.070
Dad, I was wondering
if I could borrow $17.

04:39.180 --> 04:42.150
Chris, what do you need money for?
Isn't that why you have a paper route?

04:42.251 --> 04:46.312
No, this new kid named Kyle
keeps stealing all my customers.

04:46.421 --> 04:49.720
Oh, that's terrible.
You're a wonderful paper boy, Chris,

04:49.825 --> 04:52.090
and you need to remind
your customers of that.

04:52.195 --> 04:55.596
She's right. You gotta stand up
for yourself like my great-grandfather

04:55.732 --> 04:58.257
Turn-of-the-Century
Take-on-All-Comers Griffin.

04:58.635 --> 05:01.570
All right. Put 'em up. Put 'em up.
Are you having a bully day?

05:01.672 --> 05:04.197
I'm having a bully day.
Is everyone having a bully day?

05:04.308 --> 05:05.275
- Bully.
- Bully.

05:05.376 --> 05:08.573
- Yes, bully.
- Oh, thank God we live in this time.

05:12.917 --> 05:16.375
- Stewie, what are you doing?
- Just getting my bronze on, baby.

05:16.488 --> 05:19.355
Hey, what do you think
of my recumbent tan pose?

05:19.891 --> 05:23.453
Legs probably spread a little wider than
they ought to be, but who gives a damn.

05:23.562 --> 05:27.555
This is just Tanned Stewie
being Tanned Stewie. Check me out, Brian.

05:37.010 --> 05:39.478
Hey, Mr. Herbert. I want you back.

05:39.579 --> 05:42.047
Please, will you be
my paper-customer again?

05:42.150 --> 05:45.745
Oh, hey, Chris. Oh, is that my phone?

05:49.991 --> 05:51.481
Oh, better go get that.

05:51.592 --> 05:55.290
- Well, if it isn't King Lard Ass.
- Hey, don't call me names, Kyle.

05:55.397 --> 05:57.024
Hi, Kyle.

06:00.035 --> 06:03.597
Well, listen. It was wrong of you
to steal my customer away from me.

06:03.707 --> 06:05.140
And I want him back.

06:05.241 --> 06:06.572
Oh, yeah?

06:08.011 --> 06:09.808
Look, Griffin got his ass kicked.

06:10.246 --> 06:13.045
- What a loser!
- I have that shirt at home.

06:15.219 --> 06:16.584
You pushed me.

06:16.687 --> 06:21.784
Boys, boys. We can settle this
like reasonable and sexy teenagers.

06:21.926 --> 06:25.761
Whoever can swallow
the most Tylenol PM wins.

06:33.606 --> 06:37.098
- Oh, my God. Chris, what happened?
- Kyle beat me up.

06:37.243 --> 06:40.838
- You let that little punk beat you up?
- Peter, you should be more sympathetic.

06:40.947 --> 06:43.348
Remember, you had a bully too
when you were his age.

06:43.450 --> 06:47.318
Yeah, you're right. Randy Fulcher
used to pants me every chance he got.

06:48.455 --> 06:51.015
My book report is on the giving tree.

06:51.658 --> 06:52.647
Nerd!

06:54.396 --> 06:55.727
Randy!

06:57.198 --> 06:58.187
Nerd!

06:59.934 --> 07:01.333
Randy!

07:04.206 --> 07:06.538
- Nerd!
- Randy!

07:06.976 --> 07:10.309
Peter, I think one of us should go over
and have a talk with Kyle's parents.

07:10.413 --> 07:11.471
I'll do it, Lois.

07:11.580 --> 07:14.049
Right after
a healthy breakfast of juice, toast,

07:14.151 --> 07:18.053
and store-brand imitation Frosted Flakes
featuring Terry, the Tiger.

07:18.321 --> 07:20.016
They're food!

07:23.594 --> 07:27.325
Hey, ladies. You mind if I park here?
I'll only be a few minutes.

07:27.432 --> 07:30.560
- Stewie, what is that on your lip?
- I drew a pencil moustache.

07:30.668 --> 07:33.661
I like it 'cause it's just above my lip.
The kind of moustache that says,

07:33.772 --> 07:35.467
"Yeah, I've been nude on camera.
What of it?"

07:35.574 --> 07:37.974
Come here. I'll take care of that, sweetie.

07:38.544 --> 07:40.307
It's got spit all over it.

07:40.412 --> 07:43.438
Now I know what it feels like
to have dinner with Martin Landau.

07:43.715 --> 07:48.346
What people forget about Polanski is,
Polanski wasn't the perfectionist.

07:48.922 --> 07:53.222
And pedophile or not,
he was a perfectly professional person,

07:53.326 --> 07:54.385
and punctual.

07:54.495 --> 07:57.225
Yeah. Maybe we could talk about
something else.

07:57.331 --> 08:01.563
You know, my wife and I are very involved
in Planned Parenthood

08:01.669 --> 08:05.663
which provides possibilities
for people who are underprivileged.

08:06.174 --> 08:08.199
Maybe chew your food a little, champ.

08:15.818 --> 08:17.012
Who are all these people?

08:17.119 --> 08:19.815
Oh, just a few friends over
to enjoy this gorgeous weather.

08:19.922 --> 08:21.321
Maybe take a dip in the pool.

08:21.424 --> 08:24.394
Hey, Devon, Devon, come here.
Brian, this is Devon.

08:24.495 --> 08:26.190
Devon just finished directing a movie.

08:26.296 --> 08:30.858
Yeah, it stars a little actress named
Joan Van Ark. Maybe you've heard her.

08:31.935 --> 08:34.335
- Right, possibly.
- You're talking out of your ass.

08:34.439 --> 08:39.342
It doesn't matter, Brian. I'm tan.
Hey, Brian, Brian. Look at my tan walk.

08:41.946 --> 08:45.075
- Devon, do you have a cigarette?
- Sure. And here's a copy of my last movie.

08:45.417 --> 08:48.511
<i>It's essentially Brokeback Mountain
from the point of view of the horses.</i>

08:49.955 --> 08:51.980
Hey, the sun's been up for an hour.
Shouldn't we get riding?

08:52.091 --> 08:55.061
- Are they still sleeping?
- I don't know. I'll check.

08:56.930 --> 08:59.524
- What? What? What is it?
- Oh, God! Oh, my God!

08:59.633 --> 09:02.067
- What?
- Oh, my God! Run!

09:05.840 --> 09:08.866
- Hey, there. Are you Kyle's parents?
- Yes. Can we help you?

09:08.976 --> 09:10.273
Yeah, I'm Peter Griffin.

09:10.378 --> 09:13.779
Listen, apparently your son got
into a little scrape with my kid.

09:13.881 --> 09:17.545
- Oh, dear. They're not getting along?
- Like an old guy and a midget.

09:19.488 --> 09:21.752
Sir, will you please stop staring at me?

09:21.857 --> 09:22.983
Where's the rest of you?

09:23.392 --> 09:25.554
So listen, Chris is pretty upset
about what happened.

09:25.662 --> 09:27.459
Would you mind
if I had a word with your son?

09:27.564 --> 09:29.156
Not at all. He's up in his room.

09:30.199 --> 09:33.293
Hey, there, Kyle.
Hey, I'm Chris Griffin's father.

09:33.403 --> 09:35.030
"Hey, I'm Chris Griffin's father. "

09:35.138 --> 09:37.903
Now that's not very nice.
I don't sound like that at all.

09:38.008 --> 09:40.101
You're making me sound
like Michael Stipe.

09:40.210 --> 09:43.111
Listen, I just want you to know
what you did the other day was wrong.

09:43.213 --> 09:44.737
"What you did the other day was wrong. "

09:44.848 --> 09:47.613
- You're not making this easy, Kyle.
- " You're not making this easy, Kyle.

09:47.719 --> 09:51.246
"My name's Peter Griffin.
I'm a big, fat, dumb butt-face. "

09:51.356 --> 09:52.380
Shut up, Kyle.

09:52.490 --> 09:55.186
"I'm Peter Griffin.
I'm a dorky, fat, numb-nuts. "

09:55.293 --> 09:58.092
- Kyle, I said shut up.
- You're a poop-nose.

10:19.420 --> 10:21.115
- Hey, Peter.
- Hey, what's going on?

10:21.222 --> 10:22.189
Is something wrong?

10:22.290 --> 10:25.123
No, no.
Everything's cool right now.

10:26.161 --> 10:29.858
Might be some problems later, but we'll
cross that bridge when we come to it.

10:31.266 --> 10:34.394
Hello. Peter did what?

10:34.503 --> 10:36.563
Well, I'd best be getting to work.

10:36.673 --> 10:39.972
- It's nighttime.
- Boy, you said it. All right, take it easy.

10:42.278 --> 10:44.644
Peter, you get down from that tree
this instant.

10:44.748 --> 10:46.376
No, you're going to yell at me!

10:46.484 --> 10:50.511
You're damn right, I'm going to yell at you.
You beat up a 13-year-old boy!

10:50.621 --> 10:51.849
He called me names.

10:51.956 --> 10:54.982
You're 43 and you just assaulted
our neighbor's child.

10:55.092 --> 10:57.152
This is a very serious situation.

10:57.262 --> 10:59.662
Well, maybe you should've just
had an abortion, Lois.

10:59.765 --> 11:02.063
Would that make you happy
if I was never born?

11:02.167 --> 11:04.362
- What?
- I'm going to prison, aren't I?

11:09.275 --> 11:11.402
- What are you doing?
- Got to keep the tan up.

11:11.511 --> 11:14.036
It's not a skin color. It's a lifestyle, Brian.

11:14.147 --> 11:16.776
See, you wouldn't know that
because you're white as a ghost.

11:16.884 --> 11:19.853
You're haunting this house
with your whiteness, Brian.

11:19.953 --> 11:22.251
- Hey, wake me up in 15, will you, babe?
- Fine.

11:25.359 --> 11:31.094
<i>Key Largo, Montego
Baby, why don't we go down to Kokomo</i>

11:31.533 --> 11:35.765
<i>But not too fast
'Cause Stewie takes it slow</i>

11:41.243 --> 11:42.471
Oh, crap. Stewie!

11:56.359 --> 12:00.057
Hey, buddy. I was just coming
to tell you it's time to get out.

12:00.164 --> 12:03.998
I've been in there for six-and-a-half hours,
you son of a bitch! Don't touch me!

12:04.135 --> 12:06.797
- Well, how... Can you get up?
- I'll try.

12:16.548 --> 12:20.645
I can't do it. I can't do it. Get the lotion.
Put the lotion on me.

12:22.655 --> 12:25.590
- Brian?
- Hi, Mr. Furley.

12:25.692 --> 12:26.852
This isn't what it looks like.

12:26.960 --> 12:29.327
Never mind. I'll come back later.

12:31.532 --> 12:36.162
Now be polite, Peter. Kyle's mother agreed
not to press charges if you apologize.

12:36.270 --> 12:38.205
- Hello, Lois.
- Hello, Claire.

12:38.306 --> 12:41.867
We just came by because there's
something Peter would like to say to Kyle.

12:42.744 --> 12:44.177
- Go on.
- Sorry.

12:44.312 --> 12:46.644
- Say it right, Peter.
- Oh, oh! Sorry.

12:47.048 --> 12:49.313
Thank you, Peter.
Now what do you say, Kyle?

12:49.418 --> 12:50.851
- Apology accepted.
- Good.

12:50.953 --> 12:52.978
Now why don't you patch things up
with Mr. Griffin

12:53.089 --> 12:55.114
by showing him your LEGOs, hmm?

12:55.224 --> 12:59.059
You got LEGOs? Sweet.
Lois only buys me Mega Bloks.

12:59.163 --> 13:00.528
They're the same thing, Peter.

13:00.631 --> 13:02.758
You know what, Lois?
They're not the same thing

13:02.866 --> 13:04.731
and the sooner you get that
through your thick skull,

13:04.835 --> 13:07.065
the sooner we can get
this marriage back on track.

13:07.437 --> 13:11.534
Hey, listen. Sorry about beating you up.
I felt pretty bad about it.

13:11.643 --> 13:14.043
- Hey, this look like a spaceship to you?
- Sorta.

13:14.913 --> 13:16.847
Well, I never was very good
at building things.

13:16.948 --> 13:19.474
Like that time I built
that handmade electric razor.

13:19.852 --> 13:23.049
By gluing many razor blades
to this ordinary desk fan,

13:23.155 --> 13:25.715
I'll save time in my morning routine.

13:28.862 --> 13:31.296
Lois, I've done it again!

13:36.236 --> 13:39.263
You don't have to apologize.
I would've done the same thing.

13:39.373 --> 13:41.432
I mean,
bullying makes you feel pretty cool.

13:41.943 --> 13:44.138
Yeah. I guess it was kind of cool.

13:44.245 --> 13:46.611
You know, I always used to be
the nerd getting bullied,

13:46.714 --> 13:48.649
but doing it to someone else
was pretty sweet.

13:48.750 --> 13:51.412
And the more you do it,
the sweeter it gets.

13:58.460 --> 13:59.450
Cook much?

14:00.363 --> 14:01.990
Peter, what the hell is wrong with you?

14:02.098 --> 14:04.430
What's wrong with me? You're the one
punching yourself in the face.

14:04.534 --> 14:05.523
Peter, stop it.

14:05.635 --> 14:07.432
Hey, Lois, how come
you keep punching yourself in the face?

14:07.537 --> 14:09.733
- Peter, knock it off!
- You're gonna hurt yourself.

14:10.274 --> 14:12.970
- You're getting her good.
- Hey, Stewie. Nice sunburn.

14:13.077 --> 14:14.942
You horse's ass!

14:22.153 --> 14:23.120
Ew!

14:23.221 --> 14:24.813
Hey, Brian. You want some Stewie jerky?

14:24.923 --> 14:26.390
Oh, God, that is disgusting.

14:26.491 --> 14:30.519
I'm finally starting to peel. I'm telling you,
Brian, my tanning days are over.

14:30.630 --> 14:33.827
I'm just glad I stopped before I did
any real damage to my skin.

14:33.933 --> 14:37.425
I wouldn't be so sure. I don't remember
you having that mole before.

14:37.536 --> 14:40.370
What the devil! Where did
that come from? Brian, what is that?

14:40.474 --> 14:43.068
I don't know.
Of course, your sunburn was pretty bad.

14:43.176 --> 14:45.736
I suppose it could be the C word.

14:46.113 --> 14:47.876
What the hell does that have to do
with anything?

14:47.981 --> 14:48.948
No. Cancer.

14:49.049 --> 14:51.518
Oh...
Okay, I thought you meant...

14:51.619 --> 14:54.816
It's not important. Oh, no. Cancer.

15:00.129 --> 15:02.461
Well, the mole looks benign,
but we won't know for sure

15:02.564 --> 15:05.431
whether it's cancerous
until the tests come back in a few days.

15:05.534 --> 15:07.798
A few days? I could be dead by then.

15:07.903 --> 15:11.032
Relax, Stewie. He said it looks benign.
We'll just have to wait and see.

15:11.141 --> 15:14.633
Jim Henson had a "wait and see" attitude
and look what happened to him.

15:14.744 --> 15:16.541
Now we've got wrong-sounding Muppets.

15:17.080 --> 15:19.914
- Hey, Swedish Chef.
- Oh, hey, Kermit, what's going on?

15:20.017 --> 15:21.712
- I'm hungry.
- Oh, that's no problem.

15:21.819 --> 15:24.049
I could cook you something.
You want some spaghetti?

15:24.155 --> 15:26.214
That's like my specialty in junk.

15:26.324 --> 15:28.519
Yay!

15:34.733 --> 15:38.362
Dad, what's wrong with you?
Why are you acting like such a bully?

15:38.470 --> 15:40.996
'Cause there are two kinds of people
in this world, Chris.

15:41.107 --> 15:45.100
There are bullies and there are nerds.
And there are hot Asian chicks.

15:45.211 --> 15:48.942
They'll do what you want. Oh, yeah.
Oh, yeah. You better believe it, buddy.

15:49.048 --> 15:50.914
They will do what you want.

15:51.018 --> 15:52.918
Because they know.
They know what you want.

15:53.253 --> 15:55.084
"Oh, don't be afraid. Don't be afraid.

15:55.189 --> 15:57.350
"I won't hurt you. I won't hurt you.

15:57.458 --> 15:59.358
"Me, big American man. "

15:59.626 --> 16:03.358
My point being that I'm a bully, not a nerd.
Now where was I? Oh, yeah.

16:04.566 --> 16:05.999
Dad, get away from me!

16:06.101 --> 16:07.728
- Oh, Peter's farts are coming to get you.
- Dad, stop it!

16:07.836 --> 16:09.235
- Peter's farts are coming to get you.
- Dad, come on!

16:09.337 --> 16:11.738
Here comes Peter's farts!
Coming to get you!

16:11.841 --> 16:13.741
Oh. In the kitchen, Meg?

16:17.646 --> 16:20.980
Brian, I may only have one week to live
and I've got to make the most of it.

16:21.084 --> 16:23.678
Now, I've made a list of things
I want to do before I die

16:23.787 --> 16:26.551
and you've got to help me
since this is all your fault.

16:26.656 --> 16:30.023
Visit Chicago museum of art.
Okay, we can do that.

17:05.199 --> 17:08.498
Next on your list,
you want to learn to ballroom dance.

17:12.007 --> 17:14.441
All right, if you're going to make me
do this at least let me lead.

17:14.543 --> 17:16.272
- Fine. You lead.
- All right then.

17:31.427 --> 17:33.658
- I love you.
- What? What did you say?

17:33.764 --> 17:35.698
- Olive juice.
- Olive juice?

17:35.799 --> 17:37.562
Olive juice you, too.

17:38.102 --> 17:42.005
All right. Next up, you want to star
in a national TV commercial.

17:42.107 --> 17:45.167
If you're like me,
you suffer from chronic back pain.

17:46.945 --> 17:48.879
<i>Oh-oh, back pain.</i>

17:48.980 --> 17:50.538
<i>And chronic neck pain.</i>

17:51.182 --> 17:53.708
<i>Uh-oh. Neck pain.</i>

17:53.819 --> 17:55.411
<i>Or the occasional wrist pain.</i>

17:56.956 --> 17:58.287
<i>One of those parasites</i>

17:58.390 --> 18:01.223
<i>that swims up your crank
and starts eating away in there.</i>

18:01.327 --> 18:04.491
What? No. No, I don't have one of those.
Just the wrist thing.

18:04.598 --> 18:06.065
<i>No, it's in there.</i>

18:06.166 --> 18:08.532
<i>- Did you go swimming last week?
- Yes.</i>

18:08.635 --> 18:11.536
<i>- Did you pee in the river?
- Yes.</i>

18:11.671 --> 18:14.436
<i>- You got one.
- Oh, my God! Oh, my God!</i>

18:14.542 --> 18:18.979
<i>- I'm just kidding. It's only your wrist.
- What? You suck.</i>

18:19.080 --> 18:21.981
You're supposed to use your deep voice
for good, not evil.

18:22.083 --> 18:23.551
You suck, man.

18:25.754 --> 18:27.779
Hey, you nerds want to see
a puppet show?

18:27.890 --> 18:29.221
Peter, put me down.

18:29.324 --> 18:31.189
I told you not until you sing.

18:31.326 --> 18:33.761
<i>High on a hill
was a lonely goatherd...</i>

18:36.666 --> 18:41.228
- Dad, what are you doing to Mr. Swanson?
- Peter, put him down right now.

18:41.337 --> 18:44.569
- Beat it, Lois.
- Peter, stop it. Joe is your friend.

18:44.675 --> 18:47.508
- Shut up, you nerd.
- Hey.

18:47.611 --> 18:51.980
Peter, look at yourself. You're no different
than that bully who used to pick on you.

18:52.082 --> 18:54.415
Are you kidding?
I'm nothing like Randy Fulcher.

18:54.519 --> 18:56.714
Oh, no? Does that look familiar?

18:59.424 --> 19:01.483
Oh, my God. You're right, Lois.

19:01.593 --> 19:04.222
I shouldn't be bullying
the people I care about.

19:04.330 --> 19:08.266
I should be bullying Randy Fulcher.
He's the jerk in all this.

19:08.601 --> 19:10.660
Like Dick Cheney
when he was a Wal-Mart greeter.

19:11.070 --> 19:15.030
Go fuck yourself. Go fuck yourself.
Go fuck yourself.

19:19.279 --> 19:21.679
- Well, that's it for the list.
- Not quite, Brian.

19:21.782 --> 19:26.652
There's one more thing I need you to do
before I die. Write down my final thoughts.

19:26.754 --> 19:30.019
- Oh come on.
- I don't have much time.

19:32.026 --> 19:35.929
"O squiggly line in my eye fluid

19:36.031 --> 19:40.161
"I see you there lurking
on the periphery of my vision

19:40.836 --> 19:44.500
"But when I try to look at you
you scurry away

19:45.275 --> 19:47.573
"Are you shy, squiggly line?

19:48.311 --> 19:53.271
"Why only when I ignore you
do you return to the center of my eye?

19:54.418 --> 19:59.378
"O squiggly line, it's all right
You are forgiven"

20:00.558 --> 20:05.861
Hello. Oh, hi, Dr. Hartman. All right.
I'll tell him. Thanks. Bye.

20:06.098 --> 20:08.362
You don't have cancer.
You're going to be fine.

20:08.467 --> 20:11.527
Really? Oh, thank God! Oh, thank God!

20:12.037 --> 20:15.872
Wait, wait. Look, there's no reason
we can't finish the memoir anyway.

20:16.142 --> 20:18.076
Let's see what you got so far.

20:20.113 --> 20:22.980
Oh, you are just the worst type of person.

20:25.219 --> 20:26.709
Dad, what are we doing here?

20:26.820 --> 20:29.721
Chris, I'm going to show you
how to stand up to a bully.

20:29.823 --> 20:32.917
But first I'm going to show how when
I pull the drawstrings on my sweat shirt

20:33.027 --> 20:35.997
and spit out a candy bar,
I look like an anus.

20:40.935 --> 20:42.527
Ew! Ew! Ew!

20:47.243 --> 20:48.210
Hey, Fulcher.

20:49.145 --> 20:51.579
- Griffin?
- The feeling's mutual.

20:51.681 --> 20:55.049
- What are you doing here?
- I'm here to kick your ass, Fulcher.

20:55.152 --> 20:57.848
I'm going to beat you and then
my son, Chris, is going to beat you.

20:57.954 --> 21:00.445
It's going to be an old fashioned
father-son beat-off.

21:00.557 --> 21:04.392
- Wait a minute, Dad, you can't hit him.
- Yeah, I have MS.

21:04.495 --> 21:07.487
Oh, you hear that, Chris?
This guy's got a monkey scrotum

21:07.598 --> 21:10.658
and he's bragging about it.
Now you really got me mad.

21:10.768 --> 21:11.826
No, Dad.

21:23.315 --> 21:24.806
Stop!

21:26.619 --> 21:29.110
Sorry I had to do that, Dad,

21:29.222 --> 21:32.055
but you wanted me to learn
to stand up to a bully.

21:32.158 --> 21:34.217
Well, I'm standing up to you.

21:34.327 --> 21:37.058
Stop bullying people, Dad.

21:37.164 --> 21:39.325
My God. Chris, you're right.

21:39.834 --> 21:44.294
Look at me. Look what I've become.
I thought it'd feel good to be a bully,

21:44.405 --> 21:48.536
but all I did was make people feel
as bad as Randy made me feel.

21:48.643 --> 21:50.304
I'm just a big jackass.

21:50.412 --> 21:52.778
It's all right, Dad, I forgive you.

21:52.881 --> 21:56.283
As long as you promise never
to bully anyone again.

21:56.386 --> 21:58.081
I promise, Chris.

21:58.521 --> 22:00.716
I mean, you know,
unless I get really stinking drunk,

22:00.823 --> 22:03.587
in which case all you got to do is
outrun your sister.

22:03.960 --> 22:07.522
Oh, I like that. That's nice.
That's a warm family moment.

22:07.698 --> 22:10.064
I agree.
We can all learn something from that.

22:10.267 --> 22:13.794
Wocka, wocka.
Who wants to hear a funny-ass joke?

22:13.795 --> 23:14.795
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru